# Translation and i18n Implementation Guidelines

## Overview
This project uses Fluent (FTL) format for translations with the `LocalizationProvider` from `@newwork/nw-design-system`. All user-facing text must be internationalized.

## Required Languages
All components must provide translations for:
- **en-US** (English - US)
- **de-DE** (German - Germany)
- **ro-RO** (Romanian - Romania)

## Folder Structure

```
src/business-apps/<module>/<sub-module>/apps/<app-name>/
├── AppName.tsx
├── index.ts
└── _i18n/
    ├── en-US.ftl
    ├── de-DE.ftl
    ├── ro-RO.ftl
    └── index.ts
```

## Implementation Pattern

### 1. Translation Files (FTL)

Create translation files in `_i18n/` folder following Fluent syntax:

**en-US.ftl Example:**
```ftl
# Section Comments
welcome-title = Localization Example
welcome-subtitle = Testing the LocalizationProvider

# Form Labels
name-label = Your Name
date-label = Select Date

# Buttons
save-button = Save
cancel-button = Cancel

# Messages with Variables
welcome-user = Welcome, { $name }!
selected-date = Selected date: { $date }

# Plural Forms
items-count = { $count ->
    [one] { $count } item selected
   *[other] { $count } items selected
}
```

**Key Naming Convention:**
- Use kebab-case: `welcome-title`, `save-button`
- Group by section with comments
- Be descriptive and specific

### 2. Translation Index File

**_i18n/index.ts:**
```typescript
import enUS from './en-US.ftl?raw'
import deDE from './de-DE.ftl?raw'
import roRO from './ro-RO.ftl?raw'

export default {
  enUS,
  deDE,
  roRO
}
```

**Critical:** Use `?raw` suffix to import FTL files as raw strings.

### 3. Component Implementation

**Import Pattern:**
```typescript
import { useTranslation } from '@newwork/nw-design-system'
import translations from './_i18n'
```

**Hook Usage:**
```typescript
const MyComponent: React.FC<BusinessAppContextProps> = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation(translations)
  
  return (
    <Card>
      <CardTitle>{t('welcome-title')}</CardTitle>
      <p>{t('welcome-subtitle')}</p>
      <Button>{t('save-button')}</Button>
    </Card>
  )
}
```

### 4. Translation with Variables

**Simple Variables:**
```typescript
// FTL: welcome-user = Welcome, { $name }!
{t('welcome-user', { name: userName })}
```

**Multiple Variables:**
```typescript
// FTL: date-range = From { $startDate } to { $endDate }
{t('date-range', { startDate: '2025-01-01', endDate: '2025-12-31' })}
```

**Plural Forms:**
```typescript
// FTL:
// items-count = { $count ->
//     [one] { $count } item selected
//    *[other] { $count } items selected
// }
{t('items-count', { count: itemCount })}
```

## Translation Key Organization

### Recommended Sections

```ftl
# ========================================
# PAGE/APP TITLE & DESCRIPTION
# ========================================
app-title = My Application
app-description = Description text

# ========================================
# NAVIGATION & TABS
# ========================================
tab-overview = Overview
tab-details = Details

# ========================================
# FORM LABELS & PLACEHOLDERS
# ========================================
name-label = Name
email-label = Email Address
name-placeholder = Enter your name

# ========================================
# BUTTONS & ACTIONS
# ========================================
save-button = Save
cancel-button = Cancel
delete-button = Delete
add-button = Add

# ========================================
# TABLE HEADERS
# ========================================
table-header-name = Name
table-header-date = Date
table-header-status = Status

# ========================================
# MESSAGES & NOTIFICATIONS
# ========================================
success-message = Operation successful
error-message = An error occurred
